    <!--
        Where the watch is, as far as anything here can tell. Watch Face Format has no location
        source, so the time zone is all there is to go on: a zone is a wide thing to stand in,
        but it puts sunrise within a few minutes and the sun and moon within a degree or two.

        utcOffsetMinutes is the offset the zone keeps outside daylight saving. The watch adds
        dstMinutes to it when [IS_DAYLIGHT_SAVING_TIME] is set. Both are here so the offset can
        be worked out from sources that change once a day at most - before format 3 the only
        other numeric route to it is [UTC_TIMESTAMP], which changes every millisecond and drags
        the whole of the sun onto the per-frame path.

        dstMinutes is left off where it is the usual 60. Two zones differ: Lord Howe puts the
        clock forward half an hour, and Troll, on Antarctica, puts it forward two.

        The first 89 are the list the apps already offered; the rest come from IANA's
        zone1970.tab. Order matters: timeZoneCount keeps this many from the top, so the ones
        worth having survive being trimmed.
    -->
